normalized.text:
{
  "summary": "This first experiment tested the minimal baseline configuration: RNA-only modality, single profile, PCA (2000 components) as the RNA encoder, with no image processing, aggregation, or fusion. Validation accuracy of 0.485 (F1 0.464) establishes a reference performance floor, indicating that a simple dimensionality-reduction pipeline on RNA alone yields modest but non-trivial classification performance. Because no other configurations have been evaluated, it remains uncertain whether this level of accuracy reflects inherent task difficulty, a limitation of the PCA encoder, or the absence of complementary modalities, learned encoders, and aggregation strategies."
}

